.TH KWINFO-HELPER 8 "" "KWinfo 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
kwinfo\-helper \- Privileged sensor helper for KWinfo: RAPL power, MSRs, S.M.A.R.T. and GPU load
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkwinfo\-helper\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIcommand\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBkwinfo\-helper\fR reads, as root, the sensors the kernel keeps from other users, for \fBkwinfo\fR(1) and \fBkwinfo\-cli\fR(1): CPU package, core, GT, DRAM and platform power from the RAPL energy counters; core voltages, power\-limit status and package C\-state residency from model\-specific registers; S.M.A.R.T. data through \fBsmartctl\fR(8); and the engine load of Intel GPUs from the i915 performance counters. It never writes to the hardware and takes no paths or commands from its callers.
.PP
Nobody needs to run it by hand. As a D\-Bus system service (\fBserve\fR) it is started through systemd by D\-Bus activation on the first call to \fIio.github.kywa92.KWinfo.Helper\fR, and exits after two minutes without calls. polkit grants the action \fIio.github.kywa92.KWinfo.read\-sensors\fR to the active local session without a password and refuses remote and inactive sessions. Without the service, KWinfo can start the helper for one session through \fBpkexec\fR(1) (\fBstdio\fR).
.PP
The Debian package installs the service, with the helper in \fI/usr/libexec/kwinfo\fR. For the AppImage or a build from source, \fBinstall\fR copies the helper to \fI/usr/local/libexec/kwinfo\fR and writes the same files; \fBuninstall\fR removes exactly what it wrote.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS serve
\fBkwinfo\-helper serve\fR
.PP
Serve the D\-Bus system service (D\-Bus activation starts this as root)
.SS stdio
\fBkwinfo\-helper stdio\fR
.PP
Answer requests on standard input and output, one JSON message per line (KWinfo starts this through pkexec when no service is installed)
.SS probe
\fBkwinfo\-helper probe\fR
.PP
Show what the helper can read on this machine; run it as root
.SS install
\fBkwinfo\-helper install\fR
.PP
Install the helper, its systemd unit, D\-Bus files and polkit action (as root)
.SS uninstall
\fBkwinfo\-helper uninstall\fR
.PP
Remove what install added (as root)
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/usr/libexec/kwinfo/kwinfo\-helper\fR
The helper, as the package installs it.
.TP
\fI/usr/local/libexec/kwinfo/kwinfo\-helper\fR
The helper, as \fBinstall\fR copies it; \fIinstalled\-files\fR beside it lists everything \fBinstall\fR wrote.
.TP
\fIkwinfo\-helper.service\fR
The systemd unit, sandboxed and without network access: in \fI/usr/lib/systemd/system\fR from the package, in \fI/etc/systemd/system\fR from \fBinstall\fR.
.TP
\fI/usr/share/dbus\-1/system\-services/io.github.kywa92.KWinfo.Helper.service\fR
D\-Bus activation.
.TP
\fIio.github.kywa92.KWinfo.Helper.conf\fR
The D\-Bus policy (only root may own the name): in \fI/usr/share/dbus\-1/system.d\fR from the package, in \fI/etc/dbus\-1/system.d\fR from \fBinstall\fR.
.TP
\fI/usr/share/polkit\-1/actions/io.github.kywa92.KWinfo.policy\fR
The polkit action.
.TP
\fIkwinfo.conf\fR
Loads the msr module at boot: in \fI/usr/lib/modules\-load.d\fR from the package, in \fI/etc/modules\-load.d\fR from \fBinstall\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBsudo kwinfo\-helper probe\fR
Every source the helper can open, why the others are missing, and two rounds of readings.
.TP
\fBkwinfo\-cli helper\fR
What the service reads, asked the way KWinfo asks.
.TP
\fBjournalctl \-b \-u kwinfo\-helper.service\fR
The service\*(Aqs log.
.SH BUGS
Report problems at \fIhttps://github.com/kywa92/KWinfo/issues\fR and attach the file that \fBkwinfo\-cli report\fR writes.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBkwinfo\fR(1), \fBkwinfo\-cli\fR(1), \fBpkexec\fR(1), \fBpolkit\fR(8), \fBsmartctl\fR(8), \fBsystemd.exec\fR(5)
